            <ArticleTitle>Depression, night terrors, and insomnia associated with long-term intrathecal clonidine therapy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>36-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Intraspinal clonidine is an effective adjunct to intrathecal/epidural opioid administration. We report a case of neuropathic pain treated with intraspinal analgesics in which depression, insomnia, and night terrors developed in association with intraspinal clonidine.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
